    "summary": "This PR replaces the previous offset-based pagination in the Livewire chat UI with a cursor/window model: `Chat` gains `loadOlder()`, `loadNewer()`, `jumpToMessage()`, `loadLatestWindow()` plus cursor/canLoad* state, and `loadMore()`/`loadMessages()` become legacy aliases. The Alpine code in `chat/partials/body.blade.php` is rewritten around anchor-based scroll restoration, in-flight guards and a jump/target retry loop, and the tests are extended. Reviewers should focus on the interaction between the new server-side flags (`canLoadOlder`, `canLoadNewer`, cursors) and the client-side flags (`loadingOlder`, `pendingPrependRestore`, `initializing`), since the two sides must stay in lockstep or pagination can permanently stall.",
